      "content": "Those are good, thanks. The second one is definitely the vibe I'm going for.\n\nActually, one more thing—it's just so frustrating because these errors feel so... I don't know, weirdly specific? Like they aren't just big mistakes, they're these tiny, almost intentional-feeling little glitches that happen right when you think everything is fine. It's almost like there's some kind of unseen force or some little nuisance just waiting to trip us up. \n\nDo you think it's worth mentioning that feeling of these 'random glitches' in the message, or should I just stick to the professional 'data accuracy' angle? I want them to realize that even these tiny, almost invisible errors are actually a big deal.",
      "source": "evaluator"
