      "content": "Wait, did you just say \"mysterious gremlin\"? Haha, that's funny, but I didn't actually use that word. \n\nI mean, I get what you mean about it being dramatic, but it really does feel like that sometimes. It's like these little errors have a mind of their own. \n\nDoes that sound too unprofessional to include even in a casual Slack? I just want to capture that sense that these aren't just big, obvious mistakes, but these little, pesky things that just seem to exist to mess things up. I don't want to use the word \"gremlin\" or anything like that, obviously, but is there a better way to describe that feeling of a tiny, persistent irritant without being weird?",
